+## Submission
+
+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL create a new revision for that visit and store the submitted payload, author ID, base revision ID, and server receipt time.
+- [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission names a base revision ID that does not exist or is not the current revision, the system SHALL accept it and mark it as an unresolved revision awaiting coordinator review.
+- [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original revision ID and result without creating another revision.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and return an error.
+- [ ] **REC-005**: When a submission references a plot ID not in the site catalog, the system SHALL reject the submission and return an error.
+
+## Retrieval and Conflict Detection
+
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL return the current revision (most recent uncontested submission) and its fields.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a visit has unresolved competing revisions, the system SHALL include in the retrieval response the list of competing revision IDs and their authors.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a tablet requests unresolved-work summary, the system SHALL return for each visit with competing revisions the visit ID, base revision ID of the pending submission, and competing revision count.
+
+## Resolution
+
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When a coordinator selects "accept this revision" on an unresolved visit, the system SHALL mark that revision as accepted, discard other competing revisions, and record the coordinator's identity and resolution timestamp.
+- [ ] **REC-021**: When a coordinator selects "discard this revision" on a competing submission, the system SHALL remove it from the unresolved list and record the decision.
+- [ ] **REC-022**: When a coordinator manually combines competing revisions into a new edit, the system SHALL create a new revision with the coordinator's identity as author and mark contributing revisions as resolved via combination.
+- [ ] **REC-023**: When review work is resolved for a visit, the system SHALL allow that visit to be included in export candidate queries.
+
+## Audit and History
+
+- [ ] **REC-030**: When a visit's revision history is requested, the system SHALL return the complete sequence of revisions with author ID, base revision ID, receipt timestamp, and current status (accepted, discarded, or combined).
+- [ ] **REC-031**: When a revision is accepted or discarded, the system SHALL record the resolution operation with the coordinator's identity, decision type, and timestamp.
